    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d739">

                <pb facs="0733" n="1467" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1467"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr.
                            Terrell.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-01-21"><hi rendition="#italic">January 21,
                        1896</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 812.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 761, of the 6th
                    instant, inclosing the minister of foreign affairs denial of complicity of
                    Ottoman troops in the outrages at Marash.</p>
                <p>In this denial Tewfik Pasha states that the missionaries themselves sent an
                    address of thanks to the military commandant for the aid and protection afforded
                    them by the Imperial troops. The Department observes that a similar statement is
                    made in the letter of the vali of Aleppo inclosed with your No. 756, of the 4th
                    instant.</p>
                <p>Your letter to Mr. Lee, inquiring as to the circumstances under which the
                    missionaries sent their “address of thanks” and requesting a copy of it, is
                    approved.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
